# Disk cleanup — node_modules safety

**NEVER** delete, prune, or recursively clean `dist`, `out`, `build`, `.cache`, or any other paths **inside** `node_modules/` (including nested package folders like `node_modules/@scope/pkg/dist`).

## Allowed

- Delete **project-root** build artifacts only: `/.next`, `/out`, `/dist`, `/build`, `/server/dist`, Playwright reports, coverage, etc.
- Delete the **entire** `node_modules` directory, then restore with `npm ci` / `npm install` (or equivalent).
- Clean package-manager caches (`npm cache clean`, pnpm store prune) and OS temp — not package contents under `node_modules`.

## Forbidden

- `Get-ChildItem -Recurse` / globs that match `**/node_modules/**/dist` or `**/node_modules/**/out`
- Selective removal of files under `node_modules` “to free space”

When freeing disk space, target explicit project build dirs or wipe+reinstall `node_modules` as a whole.
